<h2>A steady, diversified market with its own rulebook</h2>
<p>The UK takes a consistent spread of Indian spices, mango and psyllium husk, driven partly by significant South Asian diaspora demand and partly by broader food-manufacturing use. What's changed in recent years is the regulatory environment: since Brexit, the UK runs its own import compliance system rather than the EU's.</p>

<h2>Don't treat UK and EU shipments as interchangeable</h2>
<p>This is the single most important practical point for buyers who source from us for both UK and EU delivery. The UK's Food Standards Agency and Border Force manage import compliance independently of the EU's TRACES system, and UK maximum residue limits, while similar in spirit, are set separately and can diverge from EU limits over time.</p>
<p>Tell us specifically whether a shipment is UK-bound or EU-bound, and we'll document and test against the right standard rather than assuming one clearance covers both.</p>

<h2>Mango: sea or air depends on the product</h2>
<p>Alphonso and other premium, short-shelf-life mango varieties are frequently air-freighted to the UK to preserve quality and command premium retail pricing — a different logistics conversation from our sea-freight fresh fruit lines. If mango is your interest, tell us your target variety and use case and we'll advise on the right shipping mode.</p>

